Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: HTMLparser.c
Line: 2486
Function: htmlFindEntityPrefix
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: When cmp == 0 and slen >= len, the code calls strncmp(string + soff + 1, bytes + 2, len - 1) with soff == 1. If slen == len (a normal case when the remaining input length equals the entity name length), this reads one byte past the provided buffer (requires slen >= len + 1 to be safe). This constitutes an out-of-bounds read driven by attacker-controlled input.

Source context:
